This is the classic Exercism "connect" problem. The board is a parallelogram of hexagonal cells. After stripping spaces, row i has (n + i) characters, where n is the board size.

Cell (row r, col c) is at board[r][c], where c ranges from 0 to n+r-1.

Adjacency: a cell at (r, c) is adjacent to:
- (r-1, c-1) — upper-left
- (r-1, c) — upper-right
- (r, c-1) — left
- (r, c+1) — right
- (r+1, c) — lower-left
- (r+1, c+1) — lower-right

Player X connects left and right: the left edge is column 0, the right edge is column n+r-1 (the last character of each row).
Player O connects top and bottom: the top edge is row 0, the bottom edge is row n-1 (the last row).

Implementation: BFS/DFS from the relevant edge.

